From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:44:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: resolve a disabled sampler compare to zero, not
 one

A depth-compare instruction issued against a sampler whose compare is
disabled is undefined in Vulkan, but OpenGL reaches it as a matter of
course: when a shadow sampler names an incomplete texture, Mesa substitutes
a complete 1x1 depth texture whose compare mode is the default GL_NONE, and
then requires the sample to read as zero, the R component of the (0, 0, 0, 1)
an incomplete texture is defined to return.

Metal has no way to spell "no compare" on a sampler used with
sample_compare, and MTL_COMPARE_FUNCTION_ALWAYS resolved every such sample
to one, so all seven shadow samplers of
KHR-GL46.incomplete_texture_access.sampler read back one instead of zero.
Resolve the undefined case to zero instead, the way the emulated border
compare in the same function already does with VK_COMPARE_OP_NEVER.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_sampler.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_sampler.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_sampler.c
index 40bc4d65a5988e9bead5a05b6f6e69be8c5409c8..f1404cbb0d5334a5cb2a4f9cd893bfdd207cadd6 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_sampler.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_sampler.c
@@ -65,10 +65,17 @@ pack_sampler_info(const struct VkSamplerCreateInfo *sampler_info,
       sampler_info->unnormalizedCoordinates
          ? VK_SAMPLER_ADDRESS_MODE_CLAMP_TO_EDGE
          : sampler_info->addressModeW;
+   /* A depth-compare instruction issued against a sampler whose compare is
+    * disabled is undefined in Vulkan, but it is reachable: OpenGL substitutes a
+    * complete depth texture with a default GL_NONE compare mode whenever a
+    * shadow sampler names an incomplete texture, and then requires the sample
+    * to read as zero. MTL_COMPARE_FUNCTION_ALWAYS makes every such sample read
+    * as one instead. Resolve the undefined case to zero, the same way the
+    * emulated border compare below already does. */
    enum mtl_compare_function compare =
       sampler_info->compareEnable
          ? vk_compare_op_to_mtl_compare_function(sampler_info->compareOp)
-         : MTL_COMPARE_FUNCTION_ALWAYS;
+         : MTL_COMPARE_FUNCTION_NEVER;
    enum mtl_sampler_mip_filter mip_filter =
       sampler_info->unnormalizedCoordinates
          ? MTL_SAMPLER_MIP_FILTER_NOT_MIP_MAPPED
